Transformations: names normalized to kebab-case, with the original names in
the registry; R factors rendered as labels with levels in metadata; R NA
rendered as the dedicated missing sentinel; College and Hitters row names
kept as first identifier columns name and player, other (numeric) row names
dropped; khan's list joined into one wide table with a split column; nci60's
list joined into one wide table with a label column; nyse's logical train
column rendered as 1 and 0; character columns nyse day-of-week and
publication mech declared categorical. Boston is ISLR2's version, without the
black column of MASS::Boston. A train/test partition is a final split column
with levels train and test, the training rows first where the source has two
tables: prostate's logical train column becomes split, and vowel joins
vowel.train and vowel.test; vowel's x.1 to x.10 are named x1 to x10; the
numeric row names of prostate, sa-heart, vowel and ozone are dropped. Source row order and numeric precision retained.
Source version, archive and normalized SHA-256 hashes, variable descriptions,
and dataset-specific notes are in the registry
(datasets/islr-data/registry.rktd). Upstream documentation is retained in
datasets/islr-data/provenance; the full data license text is in
datasets/islr-data/licenses.
